# Chains of Mephistopheles and Notion Thief, both Bot1's, as in the scenario beside this one, but Bot2 has Chains apply
# first to each of its Ancestral Recall draws (CR 616.1): it discards a Swamp, and so draws a card - and Notion Thief, which
# has not yet had its opportunity, replaces that draw, so Bot1 draws instead. Chains has had its opportunity at that draw
# (CR 614.5), so Bot1's draws are plain: Bot1 draws three cards and discards none; Bot2 discards three Swamps and draws
# nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Chains of Mephistopheles
Notion Thief
Forest
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Ancestral Recall
Swamp x5
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Chains of Mephistopheles.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Notion Thief.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot2)
Bot2.Replace(Chains of Mephistopheles)
Bot2.Choose(Swamp)
Bot2.Replace(Chains of Mephistopheles)
Bot2.Choose(Swamp)
Bot2.Replace(Chains of Mephistopheles)
Bot2.Choose(Swamp)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Island; Island; Island
Bot1.Library.Count = 17
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus
Bot2.Hand.Count = 3
Bot2.Library.Count = 19
Bot2.Graveyard = Ancestral Recall; Swamp; Swamp; Swamp
